## 6. Cross-Source Correlation Rules (planned)

Once AD events land in `wazuh-*`, these EQL sequences become possible:

| Rule | Detection |
|---|---|
| AD group change + Keycloak admin login | Privilege escalation via compromised AD |
| Authelia brute force + Suricata scan from same IP | Coordinated credential attack |
| Coraza WAF block + Authelia auth failure + Keycloak token request | Exploitation followed by lateral pivot |
| AD account disabled + continued Authelia auth attempts | Stale session / hijack |
| Kerberos failure across multiple hosts | Kerberoasting / pass-the-ticket |

